From 61ba1954da464765e9f70cae8b04c23e03350d2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kislaya Srivastava <kislaya@coss.org.in>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:28:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Sajag/Glific webhook scaffold for SLF WhatsApp
 integration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the confirmed portions of the 9 Jul architecture note:
- POST /api/v1/sajag/glific/webhook — new REST surface (not the Pipecat
  telephony pipeline) receiving Glific-forwarded WhatsApp reports
- Keyed HMAC phone-number hashing (app/services/sajag_hashing.py) —
  replaces the unkeyed SHA-256 pattern in knowledge_service.py, which is
  reversible for low-entropy input like phone numbers
- SajagReports Mongo collection + status workflow
  (Received -> Triaged -> Validated -> Escalated -> In-Progress ->
  Resolved -> Feedback-Sent)
- STT call-out to ai4bharat_stt_server, LLM classification call-out to
  llm_server (vLLM), both outside the Pipecat streaming pipeline since
  Glific sends discrete events, not a live audio stream
- GET/PATCH dashboard endpoints for report list/detail/status update

Explicitly NOT implemented (stubs only, loudly logged):
- message-text PII redaction (open item d, 9 Jul note)
- photo face/number-plate redaction (open item e, 9 Jul note)

Explicitly PROVISIONAL pending Glific team confirmation:
- exact webhook payload shape (open item i)
- signature/auth scheme (shared-secret header used as placeholder)
- status-update-to-citizen mechanism (open item f)
- triangulation-tier scoring location (open item h)

Verified: syntax-checked, imports cleanly, and exercised end-to-end
against an in-memory mongomock DB (auth, consent gate, hashing,
storage, list/get/patch, invalid-status handling) — see PR description
for the test transcript. Not yet tested against a real Glific payload
or a live STT/LLM instance.
